  <data name="Tutorial.S1.Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Glass in 15 minutes</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial.S1.Intro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Let us build a simple glass: seven short steps, each highlights the button you need.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial.S1.Step1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Look around: hold the middle mouse button to orbit, use the wheel to zoom.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial.S1.Step2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Circle tool: draw the glass bottom — centre and radius 40 mm.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial.S1.Step3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Push/Pull tool: pull the bottom up by 120 mm to make the glass body.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial.S1.Step4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Circle again: on the top face draw the cavity outline with radius 35 mm.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial.S1.Step5" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Push/Pull: push the cavity down by 110 mm — walls stay 5 mm thick.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial.S1.Step6" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Soften: smooth the bottom edges to make the glass look neat.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial.S1.Step7" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Paint bucket: colour the glass as you like.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial.S1.Done" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Done! The glass is ready. Try changing the sizes via the value box.</value>
  </data>
